	)
	(text "There's some fuckery here so that it can be wired for mono, or for stereo\n(Stero bypasses everything after and including the blend)\n\nMONO    blend -> low-cut -> volume -> tip  (TS or TRS lead):   2 OFF, 3 OFF, 4 OFF\nSTEREO  A -> tip, B -> ring, no blend/filter/volume  (TRS lead):   2 ON, 3 ON, 4 ON\n1 = B polarity   2 = A direct   3 = volume bypass   4 = B to ring"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 221.488 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d57e1e28-d370-4290-b0b5-e75a53c8a2ee")
	)
	(text "The voltage divider here provides a halfway point for VREF\nSo say if you have 9v in, VREF is the midpoint at 4.5v\nand the audio signal from the opamps is centered around there"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 221.234 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d93ab8b8-9047-4f6a-9e50-4d11432a5a37")
	)
	(text "PREAMP A  (gain = 1 + (R13+GAIN_A)/R12 = x2...x12, CW = more gain)"
